# Task naming (agents + Linear)

**Bare IDs are forbidden in user-facing text.** `IPI-487` means nothing without context.

## Required format

```text
{ID} · {SPEC} — {Plain English title}
```

| ✅ Good | ❌ Bad |
|---------|--------|
| **IPI-935 · COPILOT-AUTHZ-LOCAL-001 — Fix Signed-In Operator /info 403** | "the IPI-935 ticket" |
| **DEV-STAB-001 — Block combined npm run dev (fork storm)** | "do the stab ticket" |

## When writing

- **First mention** in a reply → full name (bold).
- **Roadmaps, tables, PR titles, commits** → full name every row/line.
- **Later in the same message** → plain English title only if still unambiguous.
- **Links** → markdown link label uses full name; URL may use numeric ID.

## SSOT for canonical names

| Track | Lookup |
|-------|--------|
| Mastra runtime | `docs/copilotkit-mastra/README.md`, `docs/mastra/runtime-family.md` |
| Host / Cursor load | `docs/archive/cursor/linux-audit.md` (historical evidence) |
| Any IPI task | Live Linear issue **title** |

If unsure of the title, read the SSOT or Linear before citing the ID.

## Linear issue titles

When creating or renaming issues, set **title** to the full format above (not `IPI-487` alone).
